<title>USA: Hot, dry weather dominates W Africa cocoa areas.</title>
<headline>Hot, dry weather dominates W Africa cocoa areas.</headline>
<dateline>LEXINGTON, MASS. 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dry and hot weather still dominates West African cocoa areas, forecaster Weather Services Corp said.</p>
<p>Temperatures are expected to remain above normal with highs reaching 90-100 degrees F and the outlook is for little change Thursday-Saturday.</p>
<p>The hot, dry weather will possibly stress trees in the Ivory Coast, it said.</p>
</text>
